{
  "about": "Golden vectors of a baseline's value of stamp format 2, and of format 1 for comparison. The expectations were computed independently of the code. Format 1: the format byte, the kind (2, a baseline), the fold version as a uvarint, B and W as 8 bytes big endian, the horizon as a uvarint length and its binary form, then the entries as a uvarint count and each its reference, event time and value (uvarint lengths and nanoseconds). Format 2 is format 1 with the leading byte 2, followed by the boot state: a uvarint count of boots and each its ID (uvarint length, bytes), first and last sighting (uvarint nanoseconds), in order of first appearance; a byte 0 for no collision or 1 and the collision (stale ID, observed at, newer ID, newer first seen); a uvarint count of carried sightings and each its instant and ID, sorted by instant and then ID, without repeats. Only a baseline with at least one boot has format 2. The entry is the record value of the format 1 golden vector 'a baseline whose entry keeps its boot and its basis'. 'refused' are values a reader must refuse.",
